From e38017a6c615c53fc5f5843cbd8830d43c531366 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 21:59:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 58/64] fix(done): close review-only bead on GitHub review
 decision, not just bead comments (feryn-19i0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A review-only bead's close gate looks for a fresh review-evidence comment
authored by the assignee on the BEAD. But the dispatched reviewer records its
verdict on GitHub via `gh pr review --approve/--request-changes`, never as a
prefixed bead comment — so the gate finds no evidence and returns a fatal skip.
gfork-2cw then force-clears the hook and escalates, leaving the mayor to close
by hand. This recurred on the feryn stress run (x0v3/#243, e56z), most visibly
when the PR head advanced mid-review so even a human scanning for evidence at
the dispatch-time head found nothing.

Add a GitHub-side evidence fallback: when no bead comment satisfies the gate,
resolve the PR from the review-only bead's pr_url var and check whether the PR
carries a review decision (APPROVED or CHANGES_REQUESTED — either proves the
review task was performed) submitted after the bead was assigned. The
post-assignment bound mirrors the bead-comment freshness rule so a stale
pre-dispatch review does not satisfy a fresh review task.

New git.HasReviewDecisionSince(pr, since) fetches `gh pr view --json reviews`
and returns true on any decision review newer than `since`. It fails safe: a
missing pr_url, unresolvable cwd, or any gh error yields no GitHub evidence and
preserves the existing escalate-and-hold behavior — the gate never false-closes.

Also handles the CHANGES_REQUESTED recurrence noted in the bead: the review-only
task is "review this PR", which is complete regardless of verdict, so a posted
changes-requested review now closes the bead instead of escalating.

Tests: git.HasReviewDecisionSince (fresh/stale/advance windows, non-decision
reviews ignored); done review-only gate (GitHub approval allows close, stale
decision rejected, missing pr_url falls through to escalation).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
